    {
      "index": 5,
      "id": "method",
      "heading": "Method",
      "chunks": [
        {
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "chunk_id": "s05_c01",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s05_c1_both_tests_follow_same_three_step",
          "text": "Both tests follow the same three-step recipe: choose a maximum subgraph order, estimate each sample's distribution from its subgraph statistics, and measure the distance between the two estimates.",
          "expected_role": "method",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "both",
            "tests",
            "follow",
            "same",
            "three-step",
            "recipe",
            "choose",
            "maximum",
            "subgraph",
            "order"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "chunk_id": "s05_c02",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s05_c2_distance_squared_mahalanobis_distanc",
          "text": "That distance is the squared Mahalanobis distance, which weights differences by an analytically computed covariance matrix. The only difference between the tests is the coordinates: raw graph moments, which are injective-homomorphism subgraph densities, versus graph cumulants.",
          "expected_role": "content",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "distance",
            "squared",
            "mahalanobis",
            "distance",
            "which",
            "weights",
            "differences",
            "analytically",
            "computed",
            "covariance"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "chunk_id": "s05_c03",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s05_c3_cumulants_obtained_moments_combinato",
          "text": "Cumulants are obtained from moments by a combinatorial Möbius transform over all connectivity-respecting partitions of a subgraph's edges, capturing the excess propensity of a structure beyond what its smaller pieces already predict.",
          "expected_role": "method",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "cumulants",
            "obtained",
            "moments",
            "combinatorial",
            "bius",
            "transform",
            "over",
            "all",
            "connectivity-respecting",
            "partitions"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 4,
          "chunk_id": "s05_c04",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s05_c4_because_computing_covariances_only_n",
          "text": "Because computing the covariances only needs subgraph counts up to twice the chosen order, both tests share the same computational complexity.",
          "expected_role": "content",
          "cue_keywords": [
